    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nnotify\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/przepompownia/mini-ui-messages-example in the current form shows (normal `n` and `search_count` messages) that updating existing message it does not delay the moment of its disappearance. \r\n\r\nThe example still uses the callback returned by `make_notify()` - I modified it like in #1341 but it still uses `vim.defer_fn()` to remove the message. The timer returned is not assigned anywhere so we lose control over the extension of the life of such message. \r\n\r\nProbably we need to \r\n- create `msg.rm_timer` with remove callback to the message,\r\n- on update call `msg.rm_timer:again()`,\r\n- `msg.rm_timer:stop(); msg.rm_timer = nil` on `remove()`.",
    "closed_at": "2024-11-18T11:41:45Z",
